{
  "case_id": "2021-21-328",
  "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES: KARLA A. GILBRIDE, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner. PAUL D. CLEMENT, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Karla A. Gilbride (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 2 of the Federal Arbitration Act requires that an agreement to arbitrate be enforced unless a generally applicable contract defense renders it unenforceable. But the Eighth Circuit didn't apply a generally applicable contract defense here. It applied an arbitration-specific waiver defense that requires the person asserting waiver to prove prejudice, even though prejudice isn't required to establish waiver of other contractual rights in Iowa."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Karla A. Gilbride (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sundance intentionally relinquished its contractual arbitration rights by asking a federal judge to dismiss this case and filing an answer that didn't mention arbitration. Those actions should have been sufficient for a finding of waiver, and the same actions placed Sundance in default within the meaning of Section 3."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Ms. Gilbride, could -- could I assume for a moment that we should think about this as a Section 3 case, and then, if -- if that's the way we think about it, this phrase \"in default in proceeding with such arbitration,\" does that incorporate state contract law principles?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry for interrupting you, but I still don't understand. Are you suggesting there's a default under Heritage Reporting Corporation"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But you would lose if it were estoppel, right, because doesn't Iowa law require prejudice?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Nothing in the FAA or state law supports Petitioner's proposed rule that a motion to stay litigation in favor of agreed-upon arbitration must be filed as expeditiously as possible or lost forever. To the contrary, Section 3 of the FAA directs that courts shall grant such motions in the -- unless the stay applicant is in default."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF PAUL D. CLEMENT ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WHERE DOES THIS FEDERAL COMMON LAW RULE COME FROM AS TO WHAT COUNTS AS DEFAULT?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KAGAN",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But it seems a little bit just making it up because you're drawing a line and what -- you're putting some things on one side of the line, and then you're saying, well, you don't default if you act inconsistently with your contractual rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would be tempted, perhaps wrongly, but tempted to say the following: They waited a long time, okay? Now that might be too late for them now to ask."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The vast majority of the circuits have done something relatively similar to what you're saying. They basically say, look, have you done something -- did you know about the arbitration agreement? Step one. Step two, did you do something inconsistent with it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice SOTOMAYOR",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "-- tell me why isn't that not a waiver as an intentional right of -- an intentional relinquishment of a known right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. CLEMENT",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Incentives right here, you can't ignore the incentives of the party that first defaults, that first violates the arbitration agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 79,
        "start": 79
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You in your briefs rely on Rule 15 as the proper analogy, and I just wanted to give you an opportunity to explain how you think that works and applies here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. GILBRIDE",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0003-0014",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 84,
        "start": 84
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's no place for a prejudice requirement. Even if this Court does analyze the question under Section 3, if you look at the structure of the FAA, over and over again you see indications that things should be done in a summary manner."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sundance",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0004-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And Sundance, my friend here, wants the standard to be substantial participation in discovery."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0004-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The current status quo that requires prejudice and requires the party asserting waiver to show prejudice results in delay and obstruction in the courts over and over again."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So you asked, Justice Kagan, where does this prejudice inquiry come from because it's not anywhere in the text."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "District Court",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "aa69b4e4a284aa033510dcd6df25541de416a04956274c507d389ccdb729b017",
      "evidence_id": "ev-aa69b4e4a284-0004-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The district court said, well, we don't know that the arbitrator wouldn't have decided that motion to dismiss differently, so you can't prove that you were prejudiced by the court deciding it in the first instance."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2021-21-328",
      "confidence": 0.0,
